{"evidence":[{"pdf_page":76,"quote":"Biodiversity (ESRS E4): As part of a comprehensive analysis, all the Group\u2019s own sites with an area of more than 3,200 m\u00b2 were examined for potential impacts on biodiversity in 2023 and 2024. We assessed any potential negative impacts on all of the biodiversity protected areas located within 5 kilometers of our sites. The only negative impacts identified were of a limited scope, and related primarily to noise and light pollution. Since fiscal year 2025, biodiversity aspects have been reviewed as part of the investment controlling process when deciding on locations. No direct dependencies on biodiversity, ecosystems and their functions (including ecosystem services) were identified for our business model. Therefore, there are no relevant physical, transition or systemic risks. No separate consultations with affected communities were held, as no material topics relating to such communities were identified.","source_id":"KB-B003-DHL-AR2025"}],"knowledge_status":"reference_candidate","predicate":{"canonical_key":"evidence_snippet_biodiversity","raw_key":"biodiversity"},"promotion":{"eligible":false,"reason":"requires_atomic_projection_and_independent_evidence_gate"},"provenance":{"reference_status":"deterministic_gap_repair_pending_semantic_projection","simulated":false,"source_artifact":"artifacts/scale_batch_003/mineru_targets/KB-B003-DHL-AR2025-p0076/dhl-group-annual-report-2025/auto/dhl-group-annual-report-2025.md","source_sha256":"6a10259f9d446327ef3450172647b97e45410821e7bb99a13c508265c85ccf6e"},"qualifiers":{"answer_status":"unverified_evidence_candidate","calculation_expression":null,"normalized_unit":null,"period_literal":"2025","reference_period":2025,"scope_boundary":null,"value_origin":"deterministic_gap_repair_projection"},"record_id":"fact-871a526818de286da231ddc1","record_kind":"fact","schema_version":"0.1","subject":{"document_ids":["KB-B003-DHL-AR2025"],"document_metadata":[{"company":"Deutsche Post AG","document_id":"KB-B003-DHL-AR2025","language":"English","local_path":"data/raw/scale_batch_003/dhl-group-annual-report-2025.pdf","sha256":"6de7006e8ac77aa60ae2333782ad4998213c15eb8c52c170502a8126bb0e3303","title":"DHL Group Annual Report 2025"}],"entity_label":"Deutsche Post AG","task_id":"KB-B003-GAP-REPAIR-KB-B003-DHL-AR2025-P0076-BIODIVERSITY"},"trust_tier":"C","value":"Biodiversity (ESRS E4): As part of a comprehensive analysis, all the Group\u2019s own sites with an area of more than 3,200 m\u00b2 were examined for potential impacts on biodiversity in 2023 and 2024. We assessed any potential negative impacts on all of the biodiversity protected areas located within 5 kilometers of our sites. The only negative impacts identified were of a limited scope, and related primarily to noise and light pollution. Since fiscal year 2025, biodiversity aspects have been reviewed as part of the investment controlling process when deciding on locations. No direct dependencies on biodiversity, ecosystems and their functions (including ecosystem services) were identified for our business model. Therefore, there are no relevant physical, transition or systemic risks. No separate consultations with affected communities were held, as no material topics relating to such communities were identified."}
